body:
@SoboLAN why do you consider a value formatted like `-.987` corrupted? It looks valid in PHP:
```php
var_dump((float) '-.987');
// double(-0.987)
```

> Given the monstruosity of typical Oracle stuff (because #corporate-bs ), I doubt I'll be able to install something like that.

You can use [wnameless/oracle-xe-11g](https://hub.docker.com/r/wnameless/oracle-xe-11g/) and spin up an instance locally.

> […] fully understand, but if this is happening, and can be isolated to a unit test (without a running OracleDB instance), then please try to do so.

@Ocramius, it's not a DBAL issue. The `oci` driver formats floats this way:
```php
$stmt = oci_parse($conn, 'SELECT TEST_NUMBER FROM TEST_TABLE');
oci_execute($stmt);
var_dump(oci_fetch_array($stmt));

// array(2) {
//   [0] =>
//   string(5) "-.123"
//   'TEST_NUMBER' =>
//   string(5) "-.123"
// }
```
